<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 06:46:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>European force to hold first Ukraine support exercise in Poland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-european-force-to-hold-first-ukraine-support-exercise-in-poland</link><description>
Around 2,800 troops from 10 European countries will take part in a military exercise in southeastern Poland from November 9 to 22, testing a multinational force designed to support Ukraine after a potential ceasefire. Led by France and Britain, the force aims to bolster Ukraine's security without taking on an offensive role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c45eeb4-d724-11f1-9971-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258377621895.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c45eeb4-d724-11f1-9971-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258377621895.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7960aa8-d727-11f1-94d9-975020f22ee2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 01:43:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c45eeb4-d724-11f1-9971-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258377621895.jpg">© Philippe Magoni, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian strikes kill at least 26 in Ukraine after war's longest ceasefire ends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-russian-strikes-kill-26-in-ukraine-after-longest-ceasefire-ends</link><description>
Russia killed at least 26 people in strikes on a village in southern Ukraine on Monday, including civilians collecting humanitarian aid, emergency workers and police officers. The attack came hours after a rare ceasefire ended, extinguishing hopes of progress towards peace.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d61602-d701-11f1-8594-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/c83c0482d49f8575fc0b65f32d551aa79b4d413b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d61602-d701-11f1-8594-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/c83c0482d49f8575fc0b65f32d551aa79b4d413b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8385d53c-d724-11f1-b9fb-a5172ee7d599</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 01:18:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77d61602-d701-11f1-8594-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/c83c0482d49f8575fc0b65f32d551aa79b4d413b.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261102-emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says</link><description>
Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyber attacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kind of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea04afee-d707-11f1-b1d9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-223118-224510-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea04afee-d707-11f1-b1d9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-223118-224510-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f68d6d32-d70c-11f1-a237-f95335add00f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:30:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Emergency alerts hacking 'designed to undermine trust in government', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/emergency-alerts-hacking-designed-to-undermine-trust-in-government-expert-says</link><description>
Emergency alert systems in Russia and Ukraine were hit in cyber attacks overnight, with fake warnings of possible nuclear strikes broadcast to users in both countries. The systems have since been brought back under control, though much remains unclear about the attacks, including who was responsible. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Dr Melanie Garson, Associate Professor in International Security at University College London. She says that these kind of attacks "are designed to undermine faith in the government's ability to provide trust".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea04afee-d707-11f1-b1d9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-223118-224510-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea04afee-d707-11f1-b1d9-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-223118-224510-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef2b778c-d707-11f1-8388-091b6edfc70c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:28:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU says fridge attacks 'deliberate attempt to disrupt' bloc's food supply</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-fridge-attacks-deliberate-attempt-to-disrupt-bloc-s-food-supply</link><description>
Grocery stores from Sweden to Portugal were hit Monday by a suspected cyberattack on their freezer systems, in what the EU denounced as a deliberate attempt to disrupt the bloc's food chain. Supermarkets in Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg and the Netherlands were among at least eight countries affected in the incident, which came three weeks after a cyberattack caused mass disruption in French grocery stores. Food retailers were forced to throw out produce that had spoiled or was at risk of spoiling after refrigerator temperatures soared overnight. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcd91bec-d6fb-11f1-8781-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-211244-211858-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcd91bec-d6fb-11f1-8781-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-211244-211858-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2660d18-d6fb-11f1-a834-a3d33105ee23</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 20:30:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia pummels Ukraine again after rare pause in fighting in Kherson</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-russia-pummels-ukraine-again-after-rare-pause-in-fighting-in-kherson</link><description>
Intense fighting between Russia and Ukraine has picked up again after a rare ceasefire allowed for a humanitarian mission to reach the war-torn, Russian-occupied city of Oleshky in the southern Kherson region. While Russia accused Kyiv of sending hundreds of drones toward Moscow overnight to Tuesday, Kyiv said Russia had killed dozens of civilians lining up for aid in Zaporizhzhia. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd2acd8c-d6ee-11f1-8073-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/00a4fa45277e01eb86e800974ef7e00d7a64002b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd2acd8c-d6ee-11f1-8073-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/00a4fa45277e01eb86e800974ef7e00d7a64002b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bdcc948c-d6ee-11f1-b2f8-4b7d190d8ef0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:53:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd2acd8c-d6ee-11f1-8073-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/00a4fa45277e01eb86e800974ef7e00d7a64002b.jpg">© Handout, Ukrainian Emergency Service, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Refrigeration cyberattacks highlight risks of connecting industry to the internet</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-caught-cold-fridge-cyberattack-highlights-internet-gadget-weaknesses</link><description>
Cyberattacks affecting supermarket refrigeration systems on Monday in several European countries – including Belgium, Estonia, Finland, Ireland, Luxembourg, the Netherlands and Sweden – have highlighted the risks of connecting industrial infrastructure to the internet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48dab10e-d6d0-11f1-b62d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9d184e67dc748e00594d4b7526509569de9d828e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48dab10e-d6d0-11f1-b62d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9d184e67dc748e00594d4b7526509569de9d828e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0118a4da-d6e3-11f1-ba5e-f187f555e5ea</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:29:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48dab10e-d6d0-11f1-b62d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9d184e67dc748e00594d4b7526509569de9d828e.jpg">© Fredrik SANDBERG / TT NEWS AGENCY/AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>British adventurer arrives back at mother's home after 28-year journey</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-british-adventurer-arrives-back-at-mother-s-home-after-28-year-journey</link><description>
British adventurer Karl Bushby enjoyed an emotional reunion with his mother and family on Monday, as he arrived back home after a 28-year, 50,000-kilometre trek from South America, crossing four continents on foot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a2dc2-d6db-11f1-bc19-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a2dc2-d6db-11f1-bc19-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini3-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">130d557a-d6dc-11f1-bcef-5b6dff722978</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:45:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine and Russia report fake emergency alerts after cyberattacks target apps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-and-russia-report-fake-emergency-alerts-after-cyberattacks-target-apps</link><description>
Authorities in Ukraine and Russia said their emergency alert mobile apps had been targeted by cyberattacks, with users in Ukraine receiving false warnings of an imminent nuclear threat. Moscow said that hackers had sent fake emergency alerts after gaining access to the Russian Emergency Situations Ministry’s mobile app, and that efforts were ongoing to restore the app's functionality.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30e69a66-d6cd-11f1-800e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-471ee61c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30e69a66-d6cd-11f1-800e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-471ee61c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a629f90-d6cc-11f1-b20f-673158319541</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:06:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Fresh wave of fridge cyberattacks hits European supermarkets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-fresh-wave-of-fridge-cyberattacks-hits-european-supermarkets</link><description>
Stores and supermarkets across Belgium, Luxembourg, Finland, Estonia and Sweden all reported early Monday abrupt temperature spikes in their fridges and freezers in an apparent cyberattack targeting refrigeration units. The incidents follow a similar attack that hit hundreds of supermarkets across France in October, triggering food loss and fires.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5631e158-d6bf-11f1-aa7d-61c7f4643f18</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:40:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/071116b6-d6b0-11f1-99f9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D64Y2DM.jpg">© Fredrik Sandberg, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italian journalists under police protection as threats rise across the country</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-italian-journalists-under-police-protection-as-threats-rise-across-the-country</link><description>
Italy is the European country with the largest number of journalists under police protection. There, journalism is a profession particularly susceptible to threats and intimidation, but the European Union's measures to protect press freedom are slow to be implemented. FRANCE 24's team has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb11af2-d6b9-11f1-9e68-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0bf09737.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bb11af2-d6b9-11f1-9e68-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0bf09737.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">112b5a04-d6b9-11f1-8741-83bfd1635af1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:20:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Consolidation of power': Bulgaria elects Iliana Iotova as first woman president</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261102-consolidation-of-power-bulgaria-elects-iliana-iotova-as-first-woman-president</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Monday, November 2: Bulgarian papers discuss the country's new president. In Belarus, some political prisoners are held in psychiatric wards instead of prisons. Also: Hitler's Eagle's Nest burned down. Will it be rebuilt and should it? Finally, the queen of Halloween, Heidi Klum, flaunts her most disgusting costume yet. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b1864be-d6af-11f1-8f3e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-28bd6ec2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b1864be-d6af-11f1-8f3e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-28bd6ec2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cd346f4-d68e-11f1-8e5b-63690de1f67e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 11:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Elitsa GADEVA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Former UK paratrooper Karl Bushby ends 28-year trek across jungles and frozen sea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-former-uk-paratrooper-karl-bushby-ends-28-year-trek-across-jungles-and-frozen-sea</link><description>
Former British paratrooper Karl Bushby on Monday came to the end of his 28-year trek around the world, arriving in his native city of Hull after having swum across the English Channel. His journey took him from the southern tip of Latin America up across the frozen Bering Strait before crossing through Central Asia and Europe to return home.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14df6f3c-d6b4-11f1-b571-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/148e4d6e97f932b0c02bc9f3e3fabc4fcd763aaf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14df6f3c-d6b4-11f1-b571-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/148e4d6e97f932b0c02bc9f3e3fabc4fcd763aaf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">187b7068-d6a6-11f1-b054-4f8c44edd8f0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 10:13:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14df6f3c-d6b4-11f1-b571-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/148e4d6e97f932b0c02bc9f3e3fabc4fcd763aaf.jpg">© Paul Ellis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Some schools blocked as limited youth protests resume after holidays</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-france-some-schools-blocked-as-limited-youth-protests-resume-after-holidays</link><description>
French students returning from autumn holidays blocked some high schools on Monday, November 2, determined to reinvigorate a protest movement despite government concessions during the break. FRANCE 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9a22dce-d6a2-11f1-bad3-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f04d5e3a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9a22dce-d6a2-11f1-bad3-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f04d5e3a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e618d376-d6a1-11f1-889f-fd311e97047e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 09:57:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>RSF publishes list of press freedom 'predators': 'Dictators want to silence journalists'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/rsf-publishes-list-of-press-freedom-predators-dictators-want-to-silence-journalists</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Thibaut Bruttin, Director General and Secretary-General of Reporters Without Borders (RSF), who says, “When a journalist is killed, it is everyone's right to know what is being endangered.” His warning captures the central democratic dilemma explored in this interview marking the United Nations' International Day to End Impunity for Crimes Against Journalists. As journalists confront lethal violence, imprisonment, political intimidation and increasingly hostile working environments, the struggle for press freedom has become inseparable from a more fundamental question: who controls the public's access to truth? For RSF, press freedom is not simply a journalist's right to speak, but society's right to know. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34a73f5a-d698-11f1-a86b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-081019-081929-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34a73f5a-d698-11f1-a86b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-081019-081929-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a660b42-d698-11f1-b872-9f3d80b6a168</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 09:06:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Repeated Russian bombing kills 26 people in Ukraine's Zaporizhzhia region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends</link><description>
Russian forces on Monday bombed ‌a village in Ukraine's southeastern Zaporizhzhia region, killing at least 26 people including two rescue workers, Ukrainian authorities said. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky alleged that ‌Russian forces repeatedly dropped aerial bombs ‌on a school in the village of Komyshuvakha that was being used to distribute humanitarian assistance. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e494fe4-d6e3-11f1-ac21-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T090542Z-673408585-RC266OAL7JNA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EVACUATION-ZAPORIZHZHIA-REGION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e494fe4-d6e3-11f1-ac21-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T090542Z-673408585-RC266OAL7JNA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EVACUATION-ZAPORIZHZHIA-REGION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">372e232e-d684-11f1-bcc0-a99176443041</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:19:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e494fe4-d6e3-11f1-ac21-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T090542Z-673408585-RC266OAL7JNA-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-EVACUATION-ZAPORIZHZHIA-REGION.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia and Ukraine accuse each other of hacking emergency alert apps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine accused each other of hacking their emergency alert applications after a local ceasefire in the war's eastern Kherson region expired on Sunday. The cyberattacks came as both sides warned of renewed fighting and Kyiv signalled it could halt strikes on Russian oil refineries in exchange for US Patriot missiles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0ced658-d65b-11f1-ae13-8b30643331f8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 01:20:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg">© Roman Pilipey, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland rocked by Constitutional showdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown</link><description>
Poland’s constitutional crisis deepened on Saturday as the European Commission urged President Karol Nawrocki to recognise new judges appointed by Prime Minister Donald Tusk. The standoff comes ahead of next year’s parliamentary election, with polls suggesting a close race between Tusk’s coalition and the nationalist right. Camille Corcoran reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a499c734-d5de-11f1-94fb-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-110736-110939-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a499c734-d5de-11f1-94fb-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-110736-110939-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a93435c2-d5de-11f1-bba3-75c6e95985cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:41:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region ends after Russia refuses extension</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end</link><description>
The longest truce of the war in Ukraine, localised in the region of Kherson, ended on Sunday after Russia refused to extend the ceasefire. The temporary pause in fighting, which began on Tuesday, enabled a humanitarian mission to the Russian-occupied town of Olechky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc18dae8-d628-11f1-82a9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305286890794.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc18dae8-d628-11f1-82a9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305286890794.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b3049c6-d5f1-11f1-b759-5fdfd5cd4c37</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 12:41:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc18dae8-d628-11f1-82a9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305286890794.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: Lula's victory, Israeli elections and Spain train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-the-week-in-pictures-lula-s-victory-israeli-elections-and-spain-train-crash</link><description>
From Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's reelection in Brazil's presidential polls, to razor-sharp margins in the Israeli general elections, to a deadly high-speed train collision in Spain, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a7640c-d43f-11f1-9207-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4FA3NA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a7640c-d43f-11f1-9207-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4FA3NA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8ce8cb4-d5dd-11f1-bc52-dfee0217a3aa</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 11:14:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8a7640c-d43f-11f1-9207-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4FA3NA.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Youth-led rallies sweep Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/youth-led-rallies-sweep-europe</link><description>
Protests in France have helped inspire youth demonstrations elsewhere in Europe, from Portugal and Italy to Germany. Germany saw particularly large rallies on Saturday, led by a youth initiative whose name roughly translates as “Gen Z has got this”. Demonstrators called for better education and healthcare, stronger climate protection and a more affordable cost of living, while also opposing any return to compulsory military service. However, protests in several major German cities turned violent towards the end of the day, particularly in the financial hub of Frankfurt. Charlotte Hughes reports on the demonstrations across Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b7566f6-d5d4-11f1-94ac-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-090621-090756-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b7566f6-d5d4-11f1-94ac-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-090621-090756-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">809a5952-d5d4-11f1-9750-353694be0e45</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 09:38:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Bulgaria's incumbent Iotova wins presidential runoff vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-bulgarians-vote-in-presidential-runoff-amid-security-tensions-in-the-black-sea</link><description>
Bulgarians on Sunday elected incumbent Preisent Iliana Iotova, a proponent of dialogue with Moscow, in a runoff race pitting her against Andrey Gyurov, a former caretaker prime minister backed by the pro-Western opposition. The vote was held as a series of drone attacks in the Black Sea heightened security concerns. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec8ce3d4-d681-11f1-9d64-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305790946625.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec8ce3d4-d681-11f1-9d64-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305790946625.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c74e3976-d5b7-11f1-9ca2-3de45c89261a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 05:47:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec8ce3d4-d681-11f1-9d64-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26305790946625.jpg">© Valentina Petrova, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Testimonies from Ukraine's Oleshky: Residents flee Russian-occupied city</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261031-testimonies-from-oleshky</link><description>
In Ukraine, some of the evacuees from the frontline city of Oleshky are beginning to tell their stories. They've been able to leave after four years of Russian occupation. American filmmaker Zarina Zabrisky has lived and reported across the Dnipro River in Ukrainian-controlled Kherson for the past three years. She's been speaking to FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee about the events of the past 24 hours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bff7a79c-d53b-11f1-8be7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26304492932574.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bff7a79c-d53b-11f1-8be7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26304492932574.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65224606-d586-11f1-928f-2f486ee77d08</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:54:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Gen Z' demonstrations across Germany demand more education funding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-german-police-protesters-clash-after-gen-z-demos</link><description>
Police and protesters clashed Saturday in Germany where tens of thousands of young people took to the streets, inspired by similar movements in other European countries. Organized by the "GenZ regelt!" ("Gen Z has got this!") group, marches were held nationwide to demand more funding for education and to protest the high cost of living.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c07ebee6-d566-11f1-b26d-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/dea6f030daee8dfc4ab2156919ce46db6d33bba1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c07ebee6-d566-11f1-b26d-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/dea6f030daee8dfc4ab2156919ce46db6d33bba1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1849522-d566-11f1-8890-95e2d3870537</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:07:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c07ebee6-d566-11f1-b26d-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/dea6f030daee8dfc4ab2156919ce46db6d33bba1.jpg">© Ralf Hirschberger, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Residents from Russian-occupied Oleshky reunite with families after evacuation operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-evacuees-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-arrive-in-ukraine</link><description>
Evacuees from Oleshky crossed into Ukrainian-held territory Saturday in a major rescue operation after travelling through Belarus during a rare truce brokered by US First Lady Melania Trump. The city of Oleshky has been under Russian occupation since 2022 and was caught in intense fighting that left residents starving and unable to leave.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bff7a79c-d53b-11f1-8be7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26304492932574.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bff7a79c-d53b-11f1-8be7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26304492932574.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">004fbab8-d529-11f1-aec2-6d88deb93bb6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:45:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bff7a79c-d53b-11f1-8be7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26304492932574.jpg">© Efrem Lukatsky, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK PM Burnham says 'open' to slavery apology but rules out financial reparations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-burnham-says-uk-open-to-slavery-apology-but-rules-out-financial-reparations</link><description>
British Prime Minister Andy Burnham said Saturday he was "open" to the UK apologising for the first time for its role in the transatlantic slave trade but rejected calls for financial reparations. Issues around Britain's colonial history have loomed large over King Charles' ongoing visit to three Caribbean nations ahead of Commonwealth summit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a003486-d527-11f1-b75d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/74706f6624812bdb75973570d6ce3acdf7330c24.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a003486-d527-11f1-b75d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/74706f6624812bdb75973570d6ce3acdf7330c24.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b4376aa-d527-11f1-82f7-c3798c38bfa4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:31:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a003486-d527-11f1-b75d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/74706f6624812bdb75973570d6ce3acdf7330c24.jpg">© Russell Cheyne, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Protesters gather at Poland's Top court</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/protesters-gather-at-poland-s-top-court</link><description>
Police in Poland have stepped up security around the country’s Constitutional Tribunal after dozens of protesters gathered on Friday to oppose the government’s suspension of its president, which they say was unlawful. Police say several people were detained after some demonstrators breached the court’s perimeter fence. Charlotte Hughes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc37982-d50c-11f1-990b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261031-100702-100845-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fc37982-d50c-11f1-990b-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261031-100702-100845-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">853769fa-d50c-11f1-879c-f51783b245e0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:31:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Polish president holds crisis talks after dramatic court standoff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261031-polish-president-holds-crisis-talks-in-court-standoff</link><description>
Poland's President Karol Nawrocki held emergency talks with political leaders on Saturday as a bitter dispute over the constitutional court escalated into a crisis over judicial independence. The row over appointing the court's judges pits Prime Minister Donald Tusk's pro-EU government against a nationalist opposition and right-wing president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75204330-d547-11f1-939a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/6718d21afb10ef1361cab530869373c2295e95cb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75204330-d547-11f1-939a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/6718d21afb10ef1361cab530869373c2295e95cb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ac2fccc-d4ca-11f1-a860-4b9c3f8852e9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:27:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75204330-d547-11f1-939a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/6718d21afb10ef1361cab530869373c2295e95cb.jpg">© Mladen Antonov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Residents leave Russian-occupied Oleshky in evacuation operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261030-residents-leave-russian-occupied-oleshky-in-evacuation-operation</link><description>
Residents evacuated from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have left for Russia's Anapa city with a Ukrainian delegation, senior official David Arakhamia said Friday. They are expected to fly to Belarus before returning to Ukraine by bus, during a rare ceasefire brokered by the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9a386dc-d4a7-11f1-91f9-57241323c8a7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:46:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bebeee6e-d4a8-11f1-b250-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4WV4NU.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Oleshky: No access to basic needs, ceasefire offers limited opportunity for humanitarian assistance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-no-access-to-basic-needs-ceasefire-offers-limited-opportunity-for-humanitarian-assistance</link><description>
Catherine Viette is pleased to welcome Jens Schumacher, Field Coordinator in Mykolaiv and Kherson with Solidarity International. Just a few kilometers separate the Ukrainian-controlled city of Kherson from Russian-occupied Oleshky. For civilians caught between military occupation, disrupted essential services and uncertain evacuation arrangements, geographical proximity offers little guarantee of access to life-saving assistance. Schumacher examines the humanitarian implications of a temporary ceasefire around Oleshky, where approximately 2,000 civilians were reported to remain. Although the cessation of attacks has created a limited opportunity for humanitarian operations, the geographical scope of the agreement, the prospects for evacuation and the possibility of sustained humanitarian access remain uncertain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6defaa90-d481-11f1-91a1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-143131-143934-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6defaa90-d481-11f1-91a1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-143131-143934-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73d178b2-d481-11f1-87b0-613a4a1fcb7d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:11:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
